# Line endings, settled here rather than left to whoever cloned this.
#
# The GitHub Actions Windows runner image sets core.autocrlf=true globally, so
# without this every text file arrives in the working tree with CRLF endings.
# Two things here would notice: golden/expected.txt is compared line for
# line by three test suites, and a shell script whose shebang ends in \r names
# an interpreter that does not exist.
#
# LF everywhere, then -- in the repository and in the working tree, on both
# platforms. MSVC, rustc and Python all read LF sources.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named rather than left to git's own detection.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
